5,1,1,talk,Mizuki,,I want to know which past projects actually worked for the people using them. Who else cares about real user satisfaction?,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Victoria,,"I’m concerned about how much disruption the timetable absorbs during construction, and whether the finished rooms are actually used afterward.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I’m curious if our delivery schedules have been consistently optimistic, or if we’re just ignoring the inevitable delays.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Kenji,,I worry the approved numbers are fiction. What does the building actually cost once it opens?,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,"I’m tired of the same few people absorbing every delay. Who else is tracking the staffing strain behind these ""efficient"" plans?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, your point about usage is key. We need to verify if the rooms are actually booked, not just built.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, exactly. We must verify actual usage against the projected demand. I will look into the booking data and the timetable records.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, that’s a solid start. I’ll examine the delivery schedules and tender records to see if our optimism is statistically justified or just wishful thinking.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, checking tenders is smart. I’ll look at renewal reserves and post-occupancy ratings to see if real costs match the paper promises.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,I’ll check staffing posts and bench technicians' routines. We need to see if the human cost is actually being ignored.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I’ll review post-occupancy ratings and survey findings. We need honest feedback on what actually worked, not just what was promised.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Victoria,,"I’ll examine the booking data for specialist and general rooms, plus the timetable records on rooms out of service.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,I’ll review the decade of delivery schedules and the weather days in the site diaries. Correlation is key here.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Kenji,,I’ll check the renewal reserve for equipment and the post-occupancy review ratings. I need to see if the real costs match the paper promises.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,I’ll examine the staffing posts since the hiring freeze and the bench technicians' weekly manual routines. The human cost is the real bottleneck.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, glad we’re aligned on post-occupancy reviews. Let’s ensure we don’t just count costs, but actual user satisfaction.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, agreed. Satisfaction is vital, but I need to confirm if the rooms are actually accessible when the work is done.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, satisfaction is lovely, but if the calendar slips, the building is just an expensive, delayed monument to our collective optimism.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, optimism is nice, but reality is expensive. I’m checking the renewal reserves and post-occupancy ratings to see the true, hidden costs.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Benjamin, monuments are for the dead. I’m checking if the living staff can actually survive the workload.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
