35,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, post-occupancy data shows shared spaces rate highest. Single-wing projects disappoint. We must prioritize accessibility over isolation.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, interesting. My data shows specialist rooms sit idle, yet we pay for off-site space to cover the gaps. That’s a massive inefficiency.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, idle rooms are a symptom, not the cause. My data shows comfort-driven projects slip a year, while inspection fixes stay on schedule.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, shared spaces win, but the equipment dies. No reserve means we pay twice. The paper costs are a lie.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, the paper lies, but the bodies break. Technicians are stuck doing manual checks because the equipment is useless.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, that manual burden is a red flag. If the equipment fails, the staff suffers. We need a plan that respects both users and workers.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, the off-site costs prove the disruption is real. We must stop building rooms that sit empty while we pay to rent space elsewhere.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shunichi, manual checks are just the visible symptom of a broken system. My weather data confirms we lose six weeks to rain, making any tight schedule a fantasy.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, rain delays are real, but the equipment rot is worse. We buy it once, then pay again to fix it. That’s the hidden tax.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Benjamin, rain is an excuse. The real failure is that we haven’t hired anyone to fix the broken systems. The freeze is a death sentence.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, the survey data confirms your fear. Hazardous materials in older blocks add months of delay. We must avoid those sites entirely.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, avoiding those sites is wise, but we must also stop creating artificial scarcity. The data shows we rent space while our own rooms sit empty.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, avoiding hazards is prudent, but ignoring the weather is negligence. Six weeks lost to rain isn’t a risk; it’s a certainty we refuse to budget for.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, avoiding hazards is smart, but ignoring the equipment rot is negligence. We buy it once, then pay again to fix it. That’s the hidden tax.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mizuki, avoiding hazards is fine, but ignoring the staffing vacuum is negligence. We can’t outsource the manual labor we refuse to hire for.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, you’re right. We can’t ignore the human cost. I’ll support any plan that relieves that burden, provided it serves shared users well.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, I agree. We must stop renting space while our own rooms sit empty. The data proves this inefficiency is unsustainable.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shunichi, I agree. We must stop pretending the calendar is flexible. If we don’t budget for the inevitable delays, we’re just setting up the next failure.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, agreed. We can’t fix what we won’t pay for. I’ll back any plan that includes a real reserve for future repairs.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mizuki, @Victoria, @Benjamin, @Kenji, thanks. Now that we agree the human cost is real, let’s see which candidate actually fixes it.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Victoria"",""Benjamin"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
