61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, Option A directly solves my data. It converts idle space into high-demand general rooms, eliminating the off-site rental costs immediately.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, Option A is a conversion, not new construction. It avoids the weather delays that plague my data. It’s the only schedule I can actually trust.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, conversions hide costs. Option D fixes the broken equipment. I need a plan that doesn’t force us to pay twice for the same failure.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mizuki, Option D is the only one that stops the bleeding. It automates the manual checks and finally relieves the technicians. I’m voting D.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, Option A is strong for shared access, but it ignores the critical safety and staffing issues. I remain committed to Option D.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, I understand your safety concerns, but my data shows the financial bleed from off-site rentals is immediate. Option A stops that loss now.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, I concede the financial point, but Option A is the only one that won’t vanish into a rainstorm. I’m voting A.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
